        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Viewing strictly by appointment only. No unauthorised access permitted. Please use the contact details provided in this listing to arrange a viewing.\r\n\r\nThe Artisan House enjoys an exceptional setting with panoramic views across Roaring Water Bay, renowned for its thirty-two islands. From this elevated vantage point, the scenery is truly striking, with the iconic Fastnet Rock visible on the horizon.\r\nThe local pier is within walking distance, making the property especially appealing to sea swimmers, boating enthusiasts, and those who enjoy fishing. Altogether, the location combines remarkable natural beauty with excellent lifestyle appeal, making it a standout feature of the property.\r\nSet on a generous 0.66 acres (2080 Sq. Mt.), the property offers ample space for outdoor activities and ensures a high degree of privacy. The extensive grounds provide a versatile area for gardening, relaxation, or entertaining, allowing residents to fully enjoy the surrounding landscape.\r\nBuilt over 20 years ago by the owner, this home represents a true labour of love. Every detail was carefully considered to ensure the design and materials harmonise with the natural surroundings. The house features a stunning local dressed stone façade and elegant white and red deal floors, enhancing its aesthetic appeal and character.  \r\nThe kitchen and living area showcase walls finished with traditional lime mortar, providing both durability and a timeless aesthetic. This classic finish contributes to the overall warmth and inviting atmosphere of the home.\r\nIn the bedrooms, demand switches are installed to create an environment conducive to restful and undisturbed sleep. These switches help maintain a harmonious setting, ensuring comfort and tranquillity throughout the night.\r\nThe property was developed on the site of the original farmyard, and the old farmhouse remains intact. This offers unlimited opportunities to expand or restore the homestead, making it an ideal setting for those seeking versatility and future potential. \r\nThe accommodation combines period charm with all the comforts of modern living, creating a unique and inviting atmosphere.  \r\nThe elegantly curved entrance opens into a warm hall with stairs leading upstairs and a door to the ground floor. The downstairs accommodation is spacious and filled with natural light, featuring a well-designed kitchen and dining area where you can relax with a coffee and take in the stunning view of Roaring Water Bay.  The kitchen/diner opens to a comfortable lounge for evening relaxation. The ground floor also includes a WC and utility room. Upstairs, there are three bedrooms and a family bathroom, one featuring a shower cubicle.\r\nThe property encompasses approximately 0.66 acres (2080 Sq. Mt.), including a spacious paddock and a well-maintained lawn at the front of the house. There is also a very sheltered area ideally suited for a kitchen garden and potpourri. The grounds feature an abundance of shrubs and plants .  The original farmhouse offers considerable versatility and may be adapted for a variety of uses.\r\nLocation & Transport: The property benefits from excellent public transport connectivity. Located just a short distance away, a local link bus service offers easy access to Skibbereen, making daily commutes or visits straightforward and efficient. In addition, Bus Éireann provides a regular service, also connecting to Skibbereen and continuing onwards to Cork City and Cork Airport. This ensures that residents have convenient options for both local and longer-distance travel., which has supermarkets, shops, restaurants, and pubs and a Secondary School.  A nearby Co-operative Store is also accessible on foot. Local schools and churches are close by. Ballydehob village is less than a ten-minute drive, and Cork City & Airport are about 90 minutes away.\r\n\r\nGeneral Disclaimer / Important Notice\r\nThese particulars are issued by Irish Rural Homes for guidance purposes only and do not form part of any contract. While every effort has been made to ensure accuracy, all descriptions, measurements, floor plans, boundaries, photographs, services, planning information and other details are approximate and should not be relied upon as statements of fact.\r\nInterested parties should satisfy themselves fully as to the condition, title, boundaries, planning status, services, fixtures, fittings and all other matters relating to the property prior to entering into any contract. The property, lands and any outbuildings are offered as seen, and no warranty is given by the vendor or selling agent in relation to their condition, suitability, use or future development potential.\r\nViewing is strictly by appointment only. No unauthorised access is permitted to the dwelling, lands or farm buildings. Please contact Irish Rural Homes using the contact details provided in this listing to arrange a suitable viewing time."
      },
